{"id": "EUVD-2026-59557", "enisaUuid": "8f1d2b12-d543-3d40-8afa-d93473882180", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtw88: fix OOB read from firmware RX descriptor exceeding DMA buffer\n\nIn rtw_pci_rx_napi(), new_len is computed as the sum of pkt_len (14-bit\ndescriptor field, max 16383) and pkt_offset (drv_info_sz + shift, both\nfirmware-controlled). The result can exceed RTK_PCI_RX_BUF_SIZE (11478),\ncausing an out-of-bounds read from the pre-allocated DMA buffer when\nskb_put_data copies new_len bytes. The USB transport already validates\nthis (rtw_usb_rx_data_put checks against RTW_USB_MAX_RECVBUF_SZ); the\nPCIe path does not.\n\nAdd a check that new_len does not exceed the DMA buffer size.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:59:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:43", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/913bd7d3d3d842b5c1d2b908a0201efa8fc79793", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/45abc14ab3f15da7d689f1a8809c1a01240a94d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08193e733e5d4790e6c937af86d78793b02709be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6a3c384393d3f0b41669ed5a2e88744aad9d87c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/26c183a86ea4dd1f2ff90c6f783649e7f5722a10", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01155ded5d4dad61840a9a3c33ab56778ef1f100", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1554fa522f16ec7c5c342ad33fe734eeb6eb2452", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e76e9ed273dfb4b3333a5ebbb94958cc5752ab6"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xfh3-hf97-85m6", "CVE-2026-74410"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0149525c-bf60-3b7e-bc3f-bbef5225b8b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3037485c68ec1a299ff41160d8fedbd4abc29b9 <45abc14ab3f15da7d689f1a8809c1a01240a94d9"}, {"id": "02a18255-ed63-368b-babc-8e0b7d6ed56b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3037485c68ec1a299ff41160d8fedbd4abc29b9 <6e76e9ed273dfb4b3333a5ebbb94958cc5752ab6"}, {"id": "1a1acd45-0e3c-3dc4-ad89-51bdffa6142e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "1cf85cb0-9644-375b-a824-5133f9b5c564", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3037485c68ec1a299ff41160d8fedbd4abc29b9 <1554fa522f16ec7c5c342ad33fe734eeb6eb2452"}, {"id": "273bb558-d947-3974-aae6-38ff8da2d219", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3037485c68ec1a299ff41160d8fedbd4abc29b9 <6a3c384393d3f0b41669ed5a2e88744aad9d87c8"}, {"id": "2d32fee4-c4ce-3554-bfd6-d4d68b87b0d1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3037485c68ec1a299ff41160d8fedbd4abc29b9 <08193e733e5d4790e6c937af86d78793b02709be"}, {"id": "353dc779-2747-3911-afe1-9f7b9cf06986", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "42a962e5-5463-3311-a4ec-6db7cc4134a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "459e148b-9d66-3ac9-a81b-2b9486da6d5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "6643c33b-8466-3b93-bab9-1b155e9ae364", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "6b101781-0ce4-3921-8d25-9e67751bb6a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "8ef8cfac-e268-33ba-b0ca-6b9a22a12d50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.2"}, {"id": "9b07504c-179b-3ec8-a2b7-5cecc23acc9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e3037485c68ec1a299ff41160d8fedbd4abc29b9 <26c183a86ea4dd1f2ff90c6f783649e7f5722a10"}, {"id": "b7f072e4-636c-381e-8506-35f663235ac5", "pro